From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:31:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wsa884x: keep the cached temperature signed

Since the accepted range was widened to the -10..150 degC trim range, a
reading below 0 degC can be cached, but temperature is unsigned, so the
hwmon reading while the PA is on wraps to about 4.29e9 millidegrees on
64-bit. Make it an int.

Fixes: 00535515e3c1 ("ASoC: codecs: wsa884x: Accept temperatures across the full trim range")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
index b1260674b62c..a2e77faacc55 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
@@ -750,7 +750,7 @@ struct wsa884x_priv {
 	 * fields: temperature and pa_on.
 	 */
 	struct mutex sp_lock;
-	unsigned int temperature;
+	int temperature;
 	bool pa_on;
 };
 
